  "text": "Sure! Here's a Python function that meets your requirements. It processes the input string by:\n\n1. Converting everything to lowercase (ignoring case).\n2. Removing punctuation.\n3. Splitting the string into words.\n4. Counting the frequency of each word using a dictionary.\n\n### \u2705 Function Implementation:\n\n```python\nimport string\n\ndef word_histogram(text):\n    # Convert text to lowercase and remove punctuation\n    text = text.lower()\n    text = text.translate(str.maketrans('', '', string.punctuation))\n    \n    # Split the text into words\n    words = text.split()\n    \n    # Count the frequency of each word\n    histogram = {}\n    for word in words:\n        histogram[word] = histogram.get(word, 0) + 1\n    \n    return histogram\n```\n\n### \ud83d\udd0d Example Usage:\n\n```python\nprint(word_histogram(\"Hello, world! Hello.\"))\n# Output: {'hello': 2, 'world': 1}\n\nprint(word_histogram(\"Python is great. Python is fun!\"))\n# Output: {'python': 2, 'is': 2, 'great': 1, 'fun': 1}\n\nprint(word_histogram(\"Test, test, TEST.\"))\n# Output: {'test': 3}\n```\n\n### \u2705 Unit Test Check:\n\nYou can now use the unit tests you provided to validate this function.\n\nLet me know if you\u2019d like this implemented in another language or with different behavior!",
